| 3 | **On Node Features for Graph Neural Networks** (Duong et al., 2019) | Foundational data-centric paper: analyzes *when and why* node features matter for GNNs, showing GNNs work well only when node features correlate strongly with labels. Proposes feature initialization methods for featureless graphs. Directly informs the hypothesis about "GNN node/edge feature counts" — tells us what features are worth engineering for polymer graphs. Transferable to polymers. |
| 4 | **Improving Subgraph-GNNs via Edge-Level Ego-Network Encodings** (Alvarez-Gonzalez et al., 2023) | Provides edge-level encodings that augment MP-GNNs with richer structural features — a data-centric approach (better features, not a new architecture). Clear ablation stories on expressivity. Informs the "edge features" dimension of the Data Centric Foundation hypothesis. Transferable to polymer multimer graphs where edge semantics (bond types, spatial relations) are critical. |

