alidation RMSE for final Testing.', 'Tg: 7170 one repeat unit p-SMILES and their corresponding Glass Transition Temperatures. Baseline: rmse=50.5 by GAT, SOTA: rmse=30.8 by PerioGT', 'PI1M(Unlabeled Dataset for Pre-training): 1 million unlabeled one repeat unit p-SMILES.'], 'active_hypotheses': ['These hypotheses carry uncertainty; as knowledge and experience accumulate, they should be continuously revised to improve the quality of the hypothesis space.', 'Data Centric Foundation (Refined): Feature engineering is the dominant factor in Tg prediction (~28K RMSE gap between basic and rich features), dwarfing multimer effects (~2.5K). Rich features (atomic number, hybridization, aromaticity, degree, formal charge, ring membership, chirality, hydrogen count) are the new minimum standard. Pure N-RU training with N≥3 is the safest and most effective multimer strategy for standard MP-GNNs using mean readout. {1,3}-RU mixed augmentation is NOT architecture-independent — it requires max-aggregation in message-passing layers (not readout) to resolve conflicting structural signals; readout-level pooling changes alone cannot rescue it.', "Advanced Algorithm Improvement (Revised after Day 2): SPSE edge-path encodings and max-aggregation are DISCONFIRMED for polymer Tg — edge-level alternative path counts are structurally zero for tree-like chains, and element-wise max causes catastrophic variance collapse in regression. LSPE's core finding reverses for polymers: static RWPE >> learned positional evolution, because topologically simple chains don't benefit from learned dynamics. Architecture scaling (4+ layers, 256+ hidden, AdamW, deeper predictor MLP) is CONFIRMED as essential — the Day 1 'preprocessing ceiling' was an undertraining artifact. Node-level positional encodings (static RWPE, k≥32 for ~104-node polymers) are CONFIRMED as the viable encoding class. Priority for Day 3-4: (a) Primary — self-supervised pretraining (PerioGT-style periodicity-aware contrastive or TransPolymer-style masked polymer modeling); (b) Secondary — further capacity scaling + polymer-specific PEs (distance-to-chain-end, monomer-index-along-backbone) optionally with GPS-style hybrid MPNN+attention. Edge-level encodings, max-aggregation, and learned positional evolution are deprioritized.", "Self-Supervised Pretraining (Day 3-4 Primary): After architecture scaling and static RWPE, the residual gap to PerioGT's 30.8K SOTA is 5.14K — this is the genuine signal that pretraining is needed (not an undertraining artifact). PI1M (~1M unlabeled polymers) is available. Promising directions: PerioGT-style periodicity-aware contrastive learning on polymer backbones, or TransPolymer-style masked polymer modeling. The simplicity principle dictates: exhaust pretraining baselines (e.g., simple masked node/edge prediction) before complex contrastive frameworks.", 'Feature-Multimer Gating Hypothesis (Emergent): The benefit of multimer augmentation is gated by feature informativeness. Testable prediction: with rich features, multimer effect size ≈ 2.5K; with standard features, effect should be smaller but measurable; with basic features, near zero. Supported by Day 1 data but formalizable with intermediate feature richness levels.', "Simplicity Principle for Polymer Graph Learning (NEW, from Day 2 meta-pattern): Simple, well-tuned baselines (rich features + architecture scaling + static node-level PEs) consistently beat complex imported mechanisms (SPSE edge paths, max-aggregation, LSPE learned evolution, GRIN mixed augmentation) for polymer Tg. This reverses the molecular GNN literature's dominant narrative. Every proposed innovation must pass a 'baseline-first' gating test: exhaust simple baselines before deploying complex mechanisms.", 'Topological Simplicity Constraint (NEW, from Day 2 structural insight): Polymer graphs (even 3-RU) are fundamentally 1D tree-like chains with sparse branching. This makes edge-level alternative path counts uniformly zero and renders learned positional evolution unnecessary. Encodings must be designed for 1D chain geometry, not generic graph topology. Node-level positional encodings (RWPE, distance-to-chain-end, monomer-index-along-backbone) are the viable class. Edge-level structural encodings requiring topological diversity are dead ends.'], 'daily_journal': [{'day': 1, 'journal': 'Day 1 — Data Centric Foundation: Ran a 4×3 factorial experiment testing multimer degree (1,2,3,{1,3}-RU) against feature richness (Basic/Standard/Rich) on the Tg dataset with GAT. Rich features dominated: ~28K RMSE improvement over basic features. Best configuration: 3-RU × Rich at 41.6K RMSE — 17.6% below the GAT baseline (50.5K). {1,3}-RU mixed augmentation failed with standard GAT, and a follow-up experiment confirmed readout-level max-pooling/L1/ELENE changes cannot rescue it. The preprocessing ceiling is established at 41.6K, leaving a 10.8K gap to SOTA (PerioGT: 30.8K). Two architecture-focused ideas generated for Day 2.'}, {'day': 2, 'journal': 'Day 2 — Advanced Algorithm Improvement: Selected and read 4 papers (GPS, LSR-MP, SPSE, LSPE). Two experiments: SPSE-MaxGAT failed — edge path counts degenerate on tree-like polymer graphs and max-aggregation caused variance collapse. LSPE-GAT partially succeeded: static RWPE k=32 reached 35.94K RMSE, while learned positional evolution degraded performance. Architecture scaling (4-layer/256hid/AdamW) alone improved baseline from 41.6K to 36.85K, revealing Day 1\'s "preprocessing ceiling" was an undertraining artifact. Gap to PerioGT SOTA (30.8K): 5.14K remaining. Established Simplicity Principle and Topological Simplicity Constraint. Generated MoMuCon and GPS-Lite ideas for Day 3.'}]}, 'connections': {}}]}

