### Summary

The PSPE experiment tested whether explicit 1D chain-geometry positional encodings (distance-to-chain-end, monomer-index-along-backbone) improve Tg prediction over the proven RWPE k=32 baseline.

**Two rounds were required.** Round 1 produced inflated results because the implementation deviated from Day 2's proven configuration (GATv2Conv→GATConv, ReLU→ELU, ReduceLROnPlateau→CosineAnnealingLR). After correction, Round 2 revealed the true PSPE effect.

### Final Results (Round 2, Corrected)

| Condition | Test RMSE (K) | Δ vs Baseline | Δ vs Day 2 Best |
|-----------|--------------|---------------|-----------------|
| baseline (RWPE k=32) | 36.98 | -- | +1.04K |
| PSPE-dce | 36.19 | -0.79K | +0.25K |
| PSPE-mi | 35.99 | -0.99K | +0.05K |
| **PSPE-combined** | **35.44** | **-1.54K** | **-0.50K** |

### Hypothesis Assessment

| Hypothesis | Verdict |
|-----------|---------|
| PSPE improves over RWPE | **CONFIRMED** — all variants improve, combined best at -1.54K |
| Chain-end physics matters (dce) | **WEAKLY CONFIRMED** — -0.79K, signal is real but modest |
| Monomer sequence matters (mi) | **WEAKLY CONFIRMED** — -0.99K, slightly stronger than dce |
| dce + mi are complementary | **CONFIRMED** — combined > max(either alone) |
| PSPE closes 1-3K of the gap | **PARTIALLY** — 1.54K is at the low end of the range |

### Key Insight

PSPE-combined sets a **new best at 35.44K** (-0.50K vs Day 2's 35.94K). The improvement is real but modest. The exponential decay in per-experiment gains (+4.75K Day 1→2, +0.91K Day 2 RWPE, +0.50K Day 3 PSPE) strongly suggests we are asymptotically approaching the non-pretraining ceiling for GAT-based architectures. The remaining **4.64K gap to SOTA (PerioGT 30.8K)** likely requires pretraining on PI1M.

