## Two Executable Ideas — Day 4 Associate Reasoning

### Idea 1: PolyBG-SSL (mem_125)
**Polymer Bond Graph Self-Supervised Pretraining**

Adapts MolCHG's bond-as-independent-node paradigm (mem_115) to polymer backbone bonds. The core insight: backbone bonds (C-C, C=C, C-O, C-N) carry chain-flexibility information currently collapsed into scalar edge attributes. A dual GAT architecture — one on the atom graph, one on the bond graph (line graph) — with bilateral cross-attention at each layer, pretrained via NT-Xent contrastive + bond-masking on PI1M.

**Key innovations**: (a) first application of bond-graph architecture to polymers, (b) BPSPE — bond-level positional encodings (distance-along-backbone), (c) multi-level pretraining combining graph-level contrastive + bond-level masking, directly instantiating the Complementary Hierarchy Principle (mem_122).

**Collapse prevention**: Explicit NT-Xent (Mechanism 3, mem_121).

---

### Idea 2: CE-JEPA (mem_126)
**Chain Ego-Net Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture**

Adapts C-FREE's contrast-free ego-net subgraph prediction (mem_118) to polymer chain topology. k-hop ego-nets along the backbone serve as local context windows (~7-15 atoms); the model predicts another ego-net's embedding (translation invariance along the chain) using EMA + Transformer predictor asymmetry. Does not require explicit negatives, large batches, or positional encodings beyond PSPE.

**Key innovations**: (a) first JEPA-style pretraining for polymer graphs, (b) dual ego-net strategy exploiting chain periodicity as a self-supervised signal, (c) size-agnostic pretraining hypothesis — 1-RU ego-nets should transfer to 3-RU because local neighborhoods are similar regardless of total chain length.

**Collapse prevention**: EMA + Transformer predictor (Mechanism 2, mem_121), validated by C-FREE on molecular graphs.

---

