| Dimension | PolyBG-SSL | CE-JEPA |
|---|---|---|
| Primary paper | MolCHG (mem_115) | C-FREE (mem_118) |
| Innovation type | Architectural (bond graph) | Pretraining paradigm (JEPA on chains) |
| Collapse mechanism | NT-Xent (explicit negatives) | EMA + predictor (asymmetric) |
| Batch requirement | ≥128 (for sufficient negatives) | ≥64 (no negatives needed) |
| VRAM sensitivity | Moderate (dual GAT) | High (3-model architecture) |
| 1-RU→3-RU transfer | Uncertain (whole-graph SSL) | Hypothesized robust (ego-net size-agnostic) |
| Risk | Bond graph may be redundant on trees | Ego-nets may be too similar on homopolymers |

Both ideas satisfy the refined Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle v2 (mem_120): they operate at the graph level, are challenging (bond-masking or ego-net complement prediction), domain-relevant (backbone chemistry, chain topology), and instantiate the Complementary Hierarchy Principle (mem_122).

