lion unlabeled one repeat unit p-SMILES.'], 'active_hypotheses': ['These hypotheses carry uncertainty; as knowledge and experience accumulate, they should be continuously revised to improve the quality of the hypothesis space.', 'Data Centric Foundation (Refined): Feature engineering is the dominant factor in Tg prediction (~28K RMSE gap between basic and rich features), dwarfing multimer effects (~2.5K). Rich features (atomic number, hybridization, aromaticity, degree, formal charge, ring membership, chirality, hydrogen count) are the new minimum standard. Pure N-RU training with N≥3 is the safest and most effective multimer strategy for standard MP-GNNs using mean readout. {1,3}-RU mixed augmentation is NOT architecture-independent — it requires max-aggregation in message-passing layers (not readout) to resolve conflicting structural signals; readout-level pooling changes alone cannot rescue it.', "Advanced Algorithm Improvement (Revised after Day 3): SPSE edge-path encodings and max-aggregation are DISCONFIRMED for polymer Tg — edge-level alternative path counts are structurally zero for tree-like chains, and element-wise max causes catastrophic variance collapse in regression. Static RWPE k≥32 is CONFIRMED as effective (+0.91K improvement), learned positional evolution (LSPE-style) is CONFIRMED detrimental. PSPE-combined (distance-to-chain-end + monomer-index-along-backbone) is CONFIRMED as incrementally beneficial, providing +0.50K over RWPE-only baseline (35.44K vs 35.94K). PSPE features are orthogonal to RWPE (max |r| < 0.35) but the improvement is modest because RWPE already captures ~75% of positional signal for topologically simple polymers. Architecture scaling (4+ layers, 256+ hidden, AdamW, deeper predictor MLP) is CONFIRMED as essential — the Day 1 'preprocessing ceiling' was an undertraining artifact. The improvement trajectory shows clear exponential decay across Days 1-3 (+4.75K → +0.91K → +0.50K), confirming the GAT-based non-pretraining asymptote 