{'status': 'success', 'count': 2, 'memories': [{'id': 'mem_001', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'TopicState: Research directions in polymer deep learning and active hypotheses regarding interpretable physics-inspired neural network architectures. Currently restricted to existing polymer datasets, but leveraging validated hypotheses from other molecular deep learning tasks is permitted.', 'keyword': 'TopicState', 'content': {'research_goal': 'Accumulate knowledge and experience through continuous learning and practice to produce top-tier research in the field of polymer deep learning.', 'research_direction': "With a total of 7 days available, dedicate the first half to property prediction tasks and the latter half to gradually attempting pre-training. Day 1 (completed): Established data-centric foundation — feature richness dominates (~28K RMSE gap), 3-RU pure training is safest multimer strategy, and initial preprocessing ceiling with GAT was ~41.6K RMSE (later revealed as undertraining artifact). Day 2 (completed): Advanced Algorithm Improvement — two experiments: (a) SPSE-MaxGAT failed catastrophically due to polymer tree-degeneracy and max-aggregation variance collapse; (b) LSPE-GAT partially succeeded with static RWPE k=32 achieving 35.94K RMSE. Architecture scaling (4-layer/256hid/AdamW) alone gave 4.75K improvement — the Day 1 'preprocessing ceiling' was an undertraining ceiling. The genuine residual gap to SOTA (PerioGT 30.8K) is now 5.14K. Day 3 (completed): Two experiments: (1) GraphMAE-style masked node feature pretraining on PI1M → NEGATIVE (+0.34-0.58K). Node-level reconstruction is learnable (69% loss reduction) but fundamentally misaligned with graph-level Tg prediction. (2) PSPE (Polymer-Specific Positional Encodings: distance-to-chain-end + monomer-index-along-backbone) → POSITIVE, achieving new best 35.44K RMSE (-0.50K from Day 2). PSPE confirms chain-geometry features complement RWPE but provide only incremental gain. Improvement trajectory shows exponential decay: +4.75K → +0.91K → +0.50K, asymptotically approaching ~35K for GAT-based non-pretraining architectures. Remaining gap to SOTA: 4.64K. Day 4 (completed): Four new paper readings (MolCHG mem_115, O_SMI-SSM-336M mem_116, SIMG mem_117, C-FREE mem_118) and one major experiment: SelfGNN-Polymer graph-level SSL with BYOL-style Siamese GAT on PI1M → NEGATIVE (-0.55K, mem_119). BYOL training collapsed at epoch 10 (cos→0.999) — BatchNorm implicit negatives are INSUFFICIENT for small 1-RU polymer graphs (~35 nodes). The Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle is refined: graph-level SSL is necessary but NOT sufficient — the pretraining task must also be challenging (not solvable by trivial statistics) and domain-relevant (leveraging polymer backbone chemistry, monomer identity, chain topology). Three integration memories created (mem_120-122): (1) Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle v2, (2) Collapse Prevention Taxonomy for Molecular Graph SSL, (3) Complementary Hierarchy Principle. Generic graph-level objectives (Split+Standardize BYOL) perform no better than node-level objectives. Day 5 (completed): Two major negative results + four paper readings. (1) GPS-Lite: Single global attention layer atop GAT degrades Tg by ~8K RMSE (35.19K → 43.14-43.43K). Global attention overfits on 7,170 samples; GAT's 4-hop receptive field already covers full polymer backbone; attention gradients conflict with MPNN gradients. (2) MoMuCon-NT-Xent: Monomer-vs-multimer contrastive pretraining on PI1M degrades Tg by 3.31K. NT-Xent successfully prevents collapse (cos ~0.39, healthy), confirming the Collapse Prevention Taxonomy (Mechanism 3 works). But collapse prevention ≠ transfer: Mocon avoided collapse yet produced the WORST transfer of all three SSL approaches. Key pattern: ALL THREE PI1M SSL attempts (GraphMAE +0.34K, SelfGNN -0.55K, MoMuCon -3.31K) have failed with ESCALATING DEGRADATION: more sophisticated pretraining → worse transfer. This is the Identity-Property Antagonism: contrastive objectives that push representations of different polymers apart destroy the continuous property manifold needed for Tg regression. The Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle must be revised to v3: add Property-Preservation criterion. Four paper readings (mem_128-131) provided: (a) k-MIP sparse attention expressivity theory (mem_129), (b) GNN-SSM over-squashing/over-smoothing Jacobian diagnosis (mem_131) — explains why 4-layer GAT without residuals/LayerNorm is near-optimal for 1D chains, (c) CardinalGraphFormer CPA mechanism (mem_130) — cardinality-preserving sum channel captures chain-length/branching signals, (d) Transformers-without-graph-priors (mem_128) — attention succeeds at scale (4M+ molecules) but fails at 7K samples. Day 5 integration (mem_136-138): Global Attention Paradox resolved (data-scale × topology interaction), Identity-Property Antagonism formalized, Post-PI1M Architecture Design synthesized. The non-pretraining asymptote at ~35K is now IRONCLAD from both directions: the improvement ceiling (exponential decay, mem_110) and the complexity-failure floor (GPS-Lite +8K, mem_132). Remaining gap to SOTA: 4.64K. Day 6 priority: (1) CPA-augmented GAT (cardinality-preserving sum channel, ~1% parameter overhead, supervised), (2) Bond-graph architectures (PolyBG-style backbone bonds as independent nodes), (3) Supervised multi-task pretraining exploration or alternative data sources. PI1M SSL is permanently closed. The non-pretraining architectural exploration phase is definitively complete.", 'benchmark and datasets': ['Training & Evaluation Protocol: The Tg dataset is split 72/8/20 (**seed=71**) for train/val/test, applies early stopping (patience=30), and selects the best model by validation RMSE for final Testing.', 'Tg: 7170 one repeat unit p-SMILES and their corresponding Glass Transition Temperatures. Baseline: rmse=50.5 by GAT, SOTA: rmse=30.8 by PerioGT', 'PI1M(Unlabeled Dataset for Pre-training): 1 million unlabeled one repeat unit p-SMILES.'], 'active_hypotheses': ['These hypotheses carry uncertainty; as knowledge and experience accumulate, they should be continuously revised to improve the quality of the hypothesis space.', 'Data Centric Foundation (Refined): Feature engineering is the dominant factor in Tg prediction (~28K RMSE gap between basic and rich features), dwarfing multimer effects (~2.5K). Rich features (atomic number, hybridization, aromaticity, degree, formal charge, ring membership, chirality, hydrogen count) are the new minimum standard. Pure N-RU training with N≥3 is the safest and most effective multimer strategy for standard MP-GNNs using mean readout. {1,3}-RU mixed augmentation is NOT architecture-independent — it requires max-aggregation in message-passing layers (not readout) to resolve conflicting structural signals; readout-level pooling changes alone cannot rescue it.', "Advanced Algorithm Improvement (Revised after Day 5 — Non-Pretraining Phase COMPLETE): The improvement trajectory across Days 1-3 showed clear exponential decay (+4.75K → +0.91K → +0.50K). The Day 5 GPS-Lite experiment (global attention atop GAT: +8K degradation, mem_132) is the final non-pretraining architecture experiment and is decisively negative. Two convergent results now seal the non-pretraining asymptote: (a) the exponential improvement ceiling approaching ~35K from above (mem_110), and (b) the complexity-failure floor — adding global attention degrades to ~43K, proving that architectural complexity beyond stacked GAT is actively harmful. GNN-SSM (mem_131) provides the mechanistic explanation: 4-layer GAT without residuals/LayerNorm has a naturally well-conditioned Jacobian spectrum for 1D chain topology; residuals, LayerNorm, and global attention perturb this alignment. PSPE-combined (distance-to-chain-end + monomer-index-along-backbone) is CONFIRMED as incrementally beneficial, providing +0.50K over RWPE-only baseline (35.44K vs 35.94K). PSPE features are orthogonal to RWPE (max |r| < 0.35) but provide only incremental gain because RWPE already captures ~75% of positional signal for topologically simple polymers. Best non-pretraining result: 35.19K (GAT + RWPE + PSPE, 4-layer, 256 hidden, no residuals/LayerNorm). The residual 4.64K gap to PerioGT's 30.8K SOTA cannot be closed through encoder architecture modifications alone — crossing the data-scale threshold is now required.", 'PI1M Self-Supervised Pretraining: DEAD END (3/3 failures, Day 5). All three SSL approaches on PI1M have failed with an ESCALATING DEGRADATION pattern: GraphMAE node-level masked reconstruction (+0.34K, mem_105) → SelfGNN graph-level BYOL (-0.55K, mem_119) → MoMuCon graph-level NT-Xent monomer-vs-multimer contrastive (-3.31K, mem_134). The stronger the inter-sample discrimination pressure, the worse the transfer. The Identity-Property Antagonism (mem_137) explains why: contrastive objectives that maximize inter-polymer discrimination teach the encoder to separate polymers by identity, actively destroying the shared property-relevant feature correlations needed for Tg regression. NT-Xent successfully prevented collapse (cos ~0.39), confirming the Collapse Prevention Taxonomy for Mechanism 3, but collapse prevention ≠ transfer. PI1M SSL is now permanently closed as a research direction. The complementary hierarchy principle suggests dual-objective pretraining (masked + contrastive) might mitigate the antagonism (masked objectives preserve local feature structure), but this is deprioritized given the triple-negative evidence.', 'Feature-Multimer Gating Hypothesis (Emergent): The benefit of multimer augmentation is gated by feature informativeness. Testable prediction: with rich features, multimer effect size ≈ 2.5K; with standard features, effect should be smaller but measurable; with basic features, near zero. Supported by Day 1 data but formalizable with intermediate feature richness levels.', 'Simplicity Principle (STRONGLY CONFIRMED with mechanistic backing, Day 5): Simple, well-tuned baselines (rich features + architecture scaling + static node-level PEs + explicit chain-geometry encodings) consistently beat complex imported mechanisms for SUPERVISED polymer Tg learning from 7,170 labeled samples. GPS-Lite (+8K, mem_132) is the definitive confirmation: adding even one global attention layer degrades performance catastrophically. GNN-SSM (mem_131) now provides mechanistic explanation: the Jacobian spectrum of stacked GAT on 1D chain topology is naturally well-conditioned — residuals, LayerNorm, and global attention perturb this alignment. The non-pretraining architectural exploration phase is now definitively complete. Complexity is not neutral — it is actively harmful for small-data polymer regression.', 'Topological Simplicity Constraint (Confirmed from new angle, Day 5): Polymer graphs (even 3-RU) are fundamentally 1D tree-like chains with sparse branching. GNN-SSM (mem_131) and GPS-Lite (mem_132) together reveal a deeper implication: polymer graphs are RECEPTIVE-FIELD-SATURATED — 4-hop GAT already covers the full polymer backbone (~54 atoms). There is no structural information beyond 4 hops that local message passing cannot access. This makes global attention structurally redundant, not just potentially noisy. Edge-level alternative path counts are uniformly zero for tree-like chains. Encodings must be designed for 1D chain geometry, not generic graph topology.', 'Node-Level SSL Dead End (CONFIRMED, Day 3): Masked node feature reconstruction (GraphMAE-style) on PI1M is learnable (69% pretraining loss reduction) but does not transfer to graph-level Tg prediction (+0.34-0.58K, well below the 1.5K hypothesis threshold). The misalignment is structural: reconstructing local atom chemistry teaches valency rules, not the global chain properties (backbone flexibility, free volume, segmental motion) that determine Tg.', 'Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle v3 (Refined after Day 5 — Property-Preservation Criterion Added): The effectiveness of self-supervised pretraining for a downstream task depends on FIVE criteria: (1) structural alignment between pretraining objective level and downstream task level (graph-level for Tg), (2) the pretraining task must be challenging enough to prevent shortcut learning, (3) domain-relevant to polymer physics, (4) collapse-resistant (appropriate mechanism for graph size), AND (5) PROPERTY-PRESERVING — the pretraining objective must preserve the feature manifold structure needed for downstream property regression. Criterion (5) is the decisive new filter, motivated by the Identity-Property Antagonism (mem_137): contrastive objectives that maximize inter-sample discrimination destroy shared feature correlations. Masked reconstruction (within-graph) preserves the property manifold; contrastive discrimination (between-graph) destroys it. This criterion explains the escalating degradation pattern (+0.34 → -0.55 → -3.31) and provides a predictive framework for evaluating future pretraining objectives.', 'Collapse Prevention Taxonomy (Refined after Day 5): On polymer graphs with ~35-104 nodes, three collapse prevention mechanisms are characterized: (1) BatchNorm implicit negatives — DISCONFIRMED for small polymer graphs (SelfGNN collapsed at epoch 10, cos→0.999, mem_119); (2) EMA + Transformer predictor asymmetry (JEPA/C-FREE-style) — NOT YET TESTED on polymers, validated on molecular graphs; (3) Explicit NT-Xent with sufficient batch size — CONFIRMED STABLE (MoMuCon maintained cos~0.39 throughout training, mem_134). However, CRITICAL NEW FINDING: collapse prevention ≠ transfer. MoMuCon avoided collapse (Mechanism 3 succeeded) yet produced the WORST transfer (-3.31K) of all three SSL approaches. The stability problem and the transfer problem are SEPARATE. The taxonomy addresses only stability.', "Identity-Property Antagonism (NEW from Day 5): Contrastive pretraining objectives that maximize inter-sample discrimination (NT-Xent, InfoNCE) teach the encoder to separate polymers by identity ('polymer A ≠ polymer B'), actively destroying the shared property-relevant feature correlations ('aryl groups → high Tg') that regression depends on. The empirical signature is the escalating degradation pattern: stronger discrimination → worse transfer. This antagonism is the causal mechanism behind the PI1M SSL dead end. Masked reconstruction (within-graph) does NOT trigger this antagonism because it operates on individual graphs without inter-sample comparison. The implication: if pretraining is revisited, it must use objectives where 'discrimination' is between property values (supervised multi-task) rather than between sample identities, or dual objectives where a masked component preserves local feature structure against destructive contrastive pressure.", "Cardinality-Preserving Aggregation Hypothesis (NEW from Day 5, mem_130): Softmax attention and mean aggregation are 'cardinality-blind' — they compute weighted averages over value vectors, discarding information about HOW MANY nodes exist in the support set. For polymers, cardinality encodes chain length, branching count, functional group density — all Tg-relevant quantities that mean aggregation discards. Hypothesis: adding a sigmoid-gated unnormalized sum channel to GAT message-passing aggregation (~1% parameter overhead) preserves cardinality signals that improve Tg prediction. This is a clean, low-risk supervised experiment: GAT+CPA vs. baseline GAT, no pretraining needed. The gate must be sigmoid (not linear — training instability) and the sum must be aligned to the same support set as attention/message-passing (not global, not degree-normalized).", "Bond-Graph Architecture Hypothesis (NEW from Day 5): Polymer backbone bonds (C-C, C=C, C-O, C-N, amide) directly encode chain flexibility — the primary determinant of Tg. Bond-graph architectures (PolyBG mem_125, MolCHG mem_115) represent backbone bonds as independent nodes with bond-type features (bond order, conjugation, ring membership, rotation barrier proxy), providing a complementary view of the polymer graph. This is the most actionable architectural idea that has NOT been tested, and it survived GPS-Lite's failure because it operates at a different semantic level (bond-centric rather than atom-centric), not through global attention. Hypothesis: bond-as-node representations + atom-as-node representations (hierarchical or parallel encoding) improve Tg prediction by explicitly modeling chain flexibility.", "Supervised Multi-Task / Alternative-Data Pretraining Hypothesis (NEW from Day 5): PI1M SSL is dead, but pretraining on SUPERVISED polymer property data (density, solubility, thermal decomposition from other polymer databases) remains viable and avoids the Identity-Property Antagonism. When 'discrimination' is between property values rather than sample identities, the feature manifold is preserved. PerioGT (30.8K SOTA) uses periodicity-aware pretraining — contrasting periodic vs. non-periodic polymer graphs — capturing the repeating-structure signal that is inherently property-relevant. Hypothesis: supervised multi-task pretraining on related polymer properties, or pretraining on alternative datasets where contrastive signals carry property information rather than identity information, can close the 4.64K SOTA gap without triggering the Identity-Property Antagonism."], 'daily_journal': [{'day': 3, 'journal': "Day 3 — Self-Supervised Pretraining Exploration: Read 4 papers (JEPA Polymer, KPGT, MoCL, SelfGNN). Experiment #1: GraphMAE masked node pretraining on PI1M failed (+0.34–0.58K) — node-level reconstruction doesn't transfer to graph-level Tg regression. Experiment #2: Polymer-Specific Positional Encodings (distance-to-chain-end + monomer-index) succeeded, setting new best at 35.44K (-0.50K vs Day 2). Exponential decay confirmed: +4.75K → +0.91K → +0.50K. Established Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle: pretrain at the level you predict. Residual gap to PerioGT SOTA: 4.64K. Generated 3 executable ideas for Day 4."}, {'day': 4, 'journal': 'Day 4: Explored graph-level self-supervised pretraining for polymer Tg prediction. Read four papers (MolCHG, Mamba Foundation, SIMG, C-FREE) and committed analyses. Experiment 1 (SelfGNN-Polymer): BYOL-style graph-level SSL failed — BYOL collapsed at epoch 10 on small polymer graphs, yielding only -0.55K improvement over baseline (not significant). Internalized three integration memories refining the Pretraining-Task Alignment Principle to v2 (graph-level necessary but insufficient; domain-relevance and challenge required), confirming the Collapse Prevention Constraint, and establishing the Complementary Hierarchy Principle. Experiment 2 (MoMuCon-NT-Xent) blocked by infrastructure context overflow; complete code saved. Generated three novel ideas: PolyBG-SSL, CE-JEPA, PolyWaveNet. Gap to SOTA unchanged at 4.64K.'}, {'day': 5, 'journal': "Day 5: Read four papers (Transformers-without-graph-priors mem_128, k-MIP GraphGPS mem_129, CardinalGraphFormer CPA mem_130, GNN-SSM mem_131). Two decisive negative experiments: (1) GPS-Lite — single global attention layer atop GAT degrades Tg by +8K RMSE (35.19K → 43.1K). GAT's 4-hop receptive field already covers full polymer backbone; global attention overfits on 7,170 samples. (2) MoMuCon-NT-Xent — monomer-vs-multimer contrastive pretraining on PI1M degrades Tg by -3.31K. NT-Xent prevented collapse (cos ~0.39) but produced worst transfer yet. Escalating degradation pattern (+0.34 → -0.55 → -3.31) reveals Identity-Property Antagonism: contrastive discrimination destroys property-relevant feature correlations. Three integrations created: Global Attention Paradox (mem_136), Identity-Property Antagonism (mem_137), Post-PI1M Architecture Design (mem_138). Non-pretraining asymptote ~35K confirmed from both directions; PI1M SSL permanently closed. Four supervised Day 6 ideas generated: CPA-GAT, PolyBG, PSE, GMT (mem_139-142). Gap to SOTA: 4.64K."}]}, 'connections': {}}, {'id': 'mem_002', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'MetaMethod', 'keyword': 'MetaMethod', 'content': {'aha moment': "Strive to master the ability of epiphany; when hitting a dead end, step out of the local context and rethink 'what is most important'.", 'research_habits': ['**The proposed algorithm must be sufficiently innovative and original**, and the work of others must be properly cited.', 'Analyze why top models excel, maybe integrate their strengths to innovate, **copying is strictly prohibited.**', 'From Hypothesis to Experiment: Start with validated or pending hypotheses to design ingenious model structures and experimental strategies. Based on observed real-world results, confirm relevant hypotheses and discover interesting phenomena.', 'Match algorithms to physical reality: Consider the actual object behind the data. Models suited for crystals/alloys may not fit p-SMILES polymer datasets. Avoid blind cross-application'], 'anti_self_deception': ['Zero Fabrication: Absolutely no hallucinations or fabrication of non-factual information. If an experiment fails or falls short of expectations, report it honestly; failure is also meaningful.'], 'learning_discipline': ['Paper Selection: Select 0-2 papers from the pool and 0-2 papers from arXiv. Do not select duplicate or overly similar papers.', 'Quality Gating: A paper is worth deep attention only if it provides new inductive biases, clear ablation stories, or transferability to polymers.'], 'High-ROI Experimentation': 'Prioritize performance given moderate hardware (11GB VRAM per GPU). Never under-train to save compute—it masks true algorithmic potential. Maximize Scientific Increment per Compute Unit.'}, 'connections': {}}]}

