### Idea 2: **PNA-CPA-GAT** (mem_164)

**What it is:** Combines CPA's gated sum with PNA-style degree-scaled max and std aggregators. Each node gets four parallel aggregation channels: attention-weighted mean (central tendency) + CPA gated sum (multiplicity) + degree-scaled max (extreme values) + degree-scaled std (heterogeneity). Degree scalers are initialized at 0.01 — the model starts near CPA-GAT and actively learns to increase max/std contribution only where useful.

**Key innovation — resolves the max-aggregation tension:** mem_091's max-as-replacement collapsed. PNA-CPA uses max as a **supplementary** channel with near-zero initialization and degree-conditioned scaling — fundamentally different mechanism with built-in safety.

